<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 2 March, from 986 to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">986 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,040 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis V becomes the last Carolingian King of the Franks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of his father Lothair, Louis V became sole king. He died a year later without an heir, and the nobles elected Hugh Capet, founder of the Capetian dynasty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1476 CE <span class="tih-ago">550 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swiss defeat Charles the Bold at Grandson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Swiss Confederates routed the Burgundian army near Lake Neuchâtel and seized Charles the Bold's rich baggage train. Further defeats at Morat and Nancy destroyed Burgundian power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1807 CE <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jefferson signs the act banning the importation of slaves</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The law prohibited bringing enslaved people into the United States from 1 January 1808, the earliest date the Constitution allowed. Smuggling and the domestic slave trade continued.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1836 CE <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texas declares independence from Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates at Washington-on-the-Brazos adopted a declaration of independence, creating the Republic of Texas. Victory at San Jacinto in April secured it, and Texas joined the United States in 1845.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1861 CE <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates the Nevada and Dakota territories</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days before leaving office, President James Buchanan signed acts organising the Nevada and Dakota territories. Nevada's silver helped finance the Union, and it became a state in 1864.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1877 CE <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rutherford B. Hayes declared winner of the disputed 1876 election</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress confirmed the Electoral Commission's award of all disputed votes to Hayes, giving him victory by one electoral vote. Under the Compromise of 1877, federal troops left the South.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1930 CE <span class="tih-ago">96 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">D. H. Lawrence dies in the south of France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The author of 'Sons and Lovers' and 'Lady Chatterley's Lover' died of tuberculosis at Vence, aged 44. 'Lady Chatterley' was not published openly in Britain until the 1960 obscenity trial.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of the Bismarck Sea begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American and Australian aircraft attacked a Japanese convoy bound for New Guinea, sinking all eight transports and four destroyers over three days. About 3,000 Japanese troops died.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1969 CE <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Concorde makes its first flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Test pilot André Turcat flew the Anglo-French supersonic airliner prototype from Toulouse. Concorde entered passenger service in 1976 and flew until 2003.</p></div></li></ol>
